lable career opportunities for Academic, Professional, and Casual staff. How to apply Frequently asked questions (FAQs) Overseas job applicants Relocation assistance Benefits of working at UNE Our New Staff Prospectus showcases our employee benefits and highlights what it is like to live and work in our UNE-based communities. Click Here to view our New Staff Prospectus UNE provides a range of competitive benefits for its employees. Working at UNE provides advantages like competitive remuneration, up to 17% employer superannuation contributions and salary packaging. Staff are offered up to twelve months paid parental leave, flexible family arrangements, excellent training and career advancement opportunities, study leave and much more. Benefits Life at UNE UNE has a well-earned reputation as one of Australia's great teaching, training and research universities with its graduates consistently rating their experience at UNE highly, a reflection of the UNE staff's commitment to student support. It is recognised as a dynamic, culturally diverse institution with increasing numbers of international and indigenous staff and students, supported by an on-campus Mosque, International office, English Language Centre and Oorala Aboriginal Centre. Living in Armidale A sophisticated and cosmopolitan city, Armidale has the very best in education, family life, lifestyle, fine dining, and sporting facilities - and no peak-hour traffic.\nUNE is the perfect place to bring up a family and enjoy a relaxed but modern lifestyle. UNE Campus The UNE campus is situated on 74 hectares of heritage parklands, overlooking the beautiful city of Armidale. All classes, residences and recreational facilities are within easy walking distance from each other. Anywhere on campus, you're only 5–10 minutes bus/bike ride from Armidale's city centre. Back to top UNE Partnerships Jobs UNE Partnerships is the wholly owned education and training company of the University of New England UNE Partnerships are always interested in hearing from talented individuals. Please email the following to Human Resources: Cover letter outlining your interested field of work. Current resume with two references. Email your CV, cover letter addressing the selection criteria and including two referees (plus other information where requested in the description) to Human Resources at hr@unep.edu.au , or call (02) 6773 0000. Work for UNEP Study Study options How to apply Fees and costs Scholarships Study online Study on campus Regional Study Centres English Language Requirements Campus Life UNE Accommodation UNE Armidale UNE Sydney UNE Tamworth UNE Taree International Why choose UNE? Study Options Study Online How to Apply Fees and Scholarships Student Visa and Conditions Contact Research Research Services Research Institutes and Centres Graduate Research School Office of the Deputy Vice-Chancellor (Research) Info For Visitors High Schools Businesses and Community Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Community Alumni Community Give to UNE Honorary and Visiting Appointments Teachers & Education Students About UNE Our University Governance Executive University Structure Faculty of Humanities, Arts, Social Sciences and Education Faculty of Medicine and Health Faculty of Science, Agriculture, Business and Law Principal Dates 2026 Annual reports News and Events Contact us Feedback Complaints Disclaimer Right to Information Privacy Accessibility Site map CRICOS Provider Number 00003G TEQSA Provider Code: PRV12054 Australian University ABN: 75 792 454 315 UNE is a member of the Regional Universities Network © University of New England, 2026 The University of New England respects and acknowledges that its\n            people, courses and facilities are built on land, and surrounded by a\n            sense of belonging, both ancient and contemporary, of the world's oldest\n            living culture. In doing so, UNE values and respects Indigenous\n            knowledge systems as a vital part of the