Reconciliation Statement Indigenous Education Statements Aboriginal Land and Sea Hub Aboriginal Art Competition Alumni Community Give to UNE Honorary and Visiting Appointments Open/close sub nav Honorary Associate, Adjunct & Clinical Appointments Visiting Academics and Research Students Teachers & Education Students About UNE Open/close sub nav Our University Open/close sub nav Our Values and Culture Strategic Plan Results and Rankings Governance Open/close sub nav Academic Board Academic Board Committees Internal Audit Chief Governance Officer and University Secretary Legal Services Records Policy and Governance Unit Compliance Contract Management Delegations Register Policies Privacy Records and Information Management Right to Information (GIPA) UNE Council University Secretariat UNE Organisational Chart Executive Open/close sub nav Vice-Chancellor Deputy Vice-Chancellor Deputy Vice-Chancellor (Research) Chief Operating Officer Chief Financial Officer Executive Director Future Students, Engagement and Technologies University Structure Faculty of Humanities, Arts, Social Sciences and Education Open/close sub nav School of Education School of Humanities, Arts and Social Sciences Faculty of Medicine and Health Open/close sub nav School of Health School of Psychology School of Rural Medicine Faculty of Science, Agriculture, Business and Law Open/close sub nav School of Environmental and Rural Science School of Law School of Science and Technology UNE Business School SABL laboratories and facilities Principal Dates 2026 Open/close sub nav Principal Dates 2027 Previous Years Joint Medical Program dates Annual reports News and Events Open/close sub nav Events Calendar Jobs at UNE Home Jobs at UNE Current Job Vacancies Current Job Vacancies The University of New England provides a family-friendly workplace, offering great staffing benefits and excellent facilities. The staff at UNE pride themselves on being able to contribute to ensuring students have the best learning experience both on campus or by long-distance education. How to apply When applying for a role with UNE, please ensure your attachments are uploaded in PDF format . Word documents cannot be accepted at this time. If you have any queries regarding this, please contact our job application team . Browse through the list of job vacancies below and click on the position title to display the job advertisement, to access the link to the position statement and the online application process. Before lodging an application please take the time to read the Preparing and submitting an application section of our website as you will find additional information there to assist you in understanding the application process at UNE. You may also like to refer to our Frequently Asked Questions . If you would like further information about a particular vacancy, please contact the nominated person listed in the advert. They will be able to answer questions in relation to the area of work, the specific requirements of the position, and to inform you about other sources of information that may be available. Disability support for applicants The University of New England is committed to providing a work environment that does not discriminate against people on the basis of disability and increasing the diversity of the workforce through the use of inclusive recruitment practices and the development of accessible workplaces. Staff disability support is facilitated through the University’s Health and Wellbeing Officer. As an applicant, if you are having difficulty with accessing the University’s on-line job application process, or you have questions about the inherent requirements of any advertised position, further information and assistance is available by emailing the Recruitment team at hr-recruitment@une.edu.au or phoning 02 6773 3705. Thank you for your interest in working at UNE. Select a vacancy type to filter the vacancies displayed [Choose one] All Vacancies Academic Staff General Staff Senior Staff Casual Staff Choose an option Display Vacancy Status Return to Current Vacancies Please note: The vacancy status will be progressively updated for all vacancies with a closing date from 1 November 2011. Unfortunately, due to time constraints we are unable to update all the vacancies prior to this date. Display Vacancy Status Study Study options How to apply Fees and costs Scholarships Study online Study on campus Regional Study Centres English Language Requirements Campus Life UNE Accommodation UNE Armidale UNE Sydney UNE Tamworth UNE Taree International Why choose UNE? Study Options Study Online How to Apply Fees and Scholarships Student Visa and Conditions Contact Research Research Services Research Institutes and Centres Graduate Research School Office of the Deputy Vice-Chancellor (Research) Info For Visitors High Schools Businesses and Community Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Community Alumni Community Give to UNE Honorary and Visiting Appointments Teachers & Education Students About UNE Our University Governance Executive University Structure Faculty of Humanities, Arts, Social Sciences and Education Faculty of Medicine and Health Faculty of Science, Agriculture, Business and Law Principal Dates 2026 Annual reports News and Events Contact us Feedback Complaints Disclaimer Right to Information Privacy Accessibility Site map CRICOS Provider Number 00003G TEQSA Provider Code: PRV12054 Australian University ABN: 75 792 454 315 UNE is a member of the Regional Universities Network © University of New England, 2026 The University of New England respects and acknowledges that its\n            people, courses and facilities are built on land, and surrounded by a\n            sense of belonging, both ancient and contemporary, of the world's oldest\n            living culture. In doing so, UNE values and respects Indigenous\n            knowledge systems as a vital part of the knowledge capital of Australia.\n            We recognise the strength, r